 ct registration deadline
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: AAAI/ACM Conference on AI\, Ethics\, and Soci
 ety\nWebsite: https://www.aies-conference.com/2026/\nSource URL: https://
 www.aies-conference.com/2026/call-for-papers/\nLocation: Malmo\, Sweden\n
 Topics: Ethics & Governance\, Fairness & Responsible AI\, Explainability 
 & Interpretability\, Robustness & Safety\nSize: M\nSubmission type: Paper
 -based / interdisciplinary\nConfidence: confirmed\nLast checked date: 202
 6-10-28\nNotes: Official AIES 2026 pages list Malmo\, Oct 12-14\, 2026\, 
 mandatory abstract pre-registration by May 14 and papers by May 21 (AoE).
  As of 2026-10-28 no 2027 edition is announced\; AAAI's AIES page lists t
 he tenth AIES with 'additional information to come'.\nScope: Ethics and s
 ocietal consequences of AI\, connecting computer science\, law and policy
 \, social science\, and philosophy. Defining concerns include governance 
 and power\, accountability after deployment\, value alignment\, fairness\
 , human-AI interaction\, and institutional practice. Technical work is re
 levant through a serious ethical or societal contribution.\nAdditional to
 pics: Human-AI Interaction & Deployment\, Privacy-preserving ML\nScope so
 urces (2026): https://www.aies-conference.com/2026/call-for-papers/\nScop
 e last checked: 2026-10-07
