SUMMARY:[Machine Learning][Learning Theory & Statistical Foundations] ACML 
 2026 - Journal-track submission deadline (OpenReview and Springer)
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: Asian Conference on Machine Learning\nWebsite
 : https://www.acml-conf.org/2026/\nSource URL: https://www.acml-conf.org/
 2026/calls/papers/\nLocation: Melbourne\, Australia\nTopics: Machine Lear
 ning\, Learning Theory & Statistical Foundations\, Explainability & Inter
 pretability\, Robustness & Safety\nSize: L\nSubmission type: Paper-based 
 / OpenReview\nConfidence: confirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-10-28\nNotes
 : Official ACML 2026 pages (checked 2026-10-28) list RMIT's Swanston Acad
 emic Building\, Melbourne\, Dec 1-4\, with all deadlines 23:59 AoE. The c
 onference track closed Jul 5 (revised) and the journal track Jun 20\, 202
 6\; the Encore track for already-published work closed Oct 25 (extended).
  Conference-track camera-ready is due Nov 1\, 2026.\nScope: Theory and pr
 actice of machine learning\, including probabilistic methods\, representa
 tion learning\, transfer and meta-learning\, reinforcement learning\, and
  learning theory. Generative models\, language models\, and trustworthy l
 earning extend this core. The broad applications list is not treated as e
 vidence that every application field defines the conference.\nAdditional 
 topics: Deep Representation Learning\, Probabilistic\, Causal & Uncertain
 ty ML\, Reinforcement Learning\, Natural Language Processing & LLMs\, Fai
 rness & Responsible AI\, Privacy-preserving ML\nScope sources (2026): htt
 ps://www.acml-conf.org/2026/calls/papers/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07
URL:https://www.acml-conf.org/2026/calls/papers/
